    {
      "id": "claim_b050e5ed2d1245cea573127ebdef2bf0",
      "statement": "The threshold editing surface in the Thresholds section is driven by the ThresholdField enum with exactly six variants — Warn, Crit, WeeklyShowAt, BarWidth, ClockMode, Layout — matching detail_len()'s return of 6 for that section; each variant has help text produced by threshold_help and shown in the status line. Numeric fields are nudged via nudge_threshold with mutual clamping (warn < crit ≤ 99, bar_width clamped 2–20), while ClockMode/Layout are enum-cycled via cycle_threshold_enum (auto→12h→24h→off and fixed→auto).",
